cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LLM-MovieLens: A Portable Pipeline and Testbed for LLM-Synthesized Item Profiles"
message: >-
  If you use this resource, please cite the paper and the archived record. The DOI
  below always resolves to the newest archived record; each archived record also
  has its own DOI, listed on its Zenodo page.
type: dataset
# No `version` here: the version belongs to the archived record on Zenodo, and a
# second place naming it is one more place to disagree.
date-released: 2026-10-30
authors:
  - family-names: Duong
    given-names: Tan Nghia
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2442-6263"
    affiliation: "Hanoi University of Science and Technology; Minastik Technology JSC"
  - family-names: Tran
    given-names: Manh Hoang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0572-2091"
    affiliation: "Hanoi University of Science and Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/minastik-ai/llm-movielens"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/minastik-ai/llm-movielens"
# The CONCEPT DOI: it resolves to the newest archived record, so a citation made
# from this file aggregates instead of splitting per record. A single record's own
# DOI is deliberately NOT a second `identifiers` entry here, because cffconvert
# emits that one in preference to this field and every generated citation would
# then split.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22766653"
# The release is SPLIT and this field says so: code, harness, datasheet, prompt
# manifest and the human-evaluation data other than six files named in LICENSE are
# CC BY 4.0; the generated profiles, their embeddings and those six files are
# CC BY-NC 4.0, reflecting the non-commercial terms of the sources they were
# generated from. Declaring only CC-BY-4.0 would tell citation tools that the data
# half permits commercial use.
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - CC-BY-NC-4.0
license-url: "https://github.com/minastik-ai/llm-movielens/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  Pipeline and evaluation harness for LLM-synthesized item profiles. A language
  model reads an item's structured metadata and writes a profile of 80-120
  requested words (95-135 realised), a 10-axis mood vector and 3-6 key themes; the harness evaluates whether the
  resulting representation outperforms the structured description consumed
  directly, under a temporal split, five seeds and full ranking. Code and
  the human-evaluation data other than six files are CC BY 4.0; the generated profiles,
  their embeddings and those six files are CC BY-NC 4.0, reflecting upstream terms.
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - large language models
  - item representation
  - MovieLens
  - resource
